{title: I Lift My Hands (Ergo Minhas Mãos) EN}
{artist: Chris Tomlin}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{c: Intro}
[G] [C] [Em] [D]

{c: Verse}
[G]Be still, there is a [C]Healer
[Em]His love is deeper than the [D]sea
[G/D]His mercy, it is [C]unfailing
[Em]His arms are a fortress for the [D]weak

{c: Pre-Chorus}
[Am7]Let faith a[C]rise
[Em]Let faith a[D]rise

{c: Chorus}
[G]I lift my hands to believe again
[Em]You are my refuge, [C]You are my strength
[G/D]As I pour out my heart, these things I remember
[Dm7]You are faithful, [C]God, forever

{c: Verse 2}
[G]Be still, there is a [C]river
[Em]That flows from Calvary's [D]tree
[G/D]A fountain for the [C]thirsty
[Em]Pure grace that washes over [D]me

{c: Bridge}
[G]Let faith arise, let faith arise
[Em]Open my [C]eyes
[C]Open my eyes
[G/D]Let faith arise, let faith arise
[F]Open my eyes, [C]open my eyes
